    "is_separate_predictors_justified": false,
    "scientific_rationale": "With N=22 independent drift scenarios across 3 datasets, fitting three separate multiclass predictors (strategy: 7 classes, generator: 4 classes, quantity regressor) yields severely insufficient statistical degrees of freedom (~3.1 samples/class). This leads to parameter instability and cross-validation variance. Conversely, the unified candidate-utility regressor evaluates N=336 candidate arms simultaneously across all scenarios, enabling consistent relative arm ranking with zero feasibility violations and lower strategy regret.",
    "architectural_recommendation": "Maintain the unified candidate-ranking architecture with ensemble regression, probability-of-acceptance gating, and deterministic rule-based supervision. Do NOT deploy separate unvalidated predictors."
